at does not fit leaves no empty layer or entry behind. Tests cover what a new layer accepts and both ways of adding layers and entries.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"andremichelle/openDAW","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:14:17Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"730ee0057aae692386e83c882a5c4a1fb8557111","github_link":"https://github.com/andremichelle/openDAW/commit/730ee0057aae692386e83c882a5c4a1fb8557111","commit_subject":"Error triage entry for live error 1193, fixed in 915902207 and marked fixed in the error log.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"andremichelle/openDAW","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:14:17Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"8db16a866be4d3a011fc7d0543fe62f1a4829158","github_link":"https://github.com/andremichelle/openDAW/commit/8db16a866be4d3a011fc7d0543fe62f1a4829158","commit_subject":"The instrument and audio effect menus get \"Wrap into Composite\". An instrument moves into the first layer of a new Instrument Composite and takes the unit's effects along. An audio effect moves into the first entry of a new FX Composite at its place in the chain, together with the other selected effects of that chain, in their order. Automation keeps following the moved devices, and the sound stays the same since a new FX Composite plays only its entries. Tape and MIDI Output cannot become layers and do not show the item. Tests cover position, order, automation, undo, nesting and the refused cases.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"expertanalytics/rasputin","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:14:10Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"80acf385d6d6cc145afc46c6f407909ad2006bd2","github_link":"https://github.com/expertanalytics/rasputin/commit/80acf385d6d6cc145afc46c6f407909ad2006bd2","commit_subject":"Record design review round 1 of h38","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"Azure/azure-sdk-tools","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-28T20:14:00Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"db0e3a8b8c11b065eed14af1d906f697d3af1830","github_link":"https://github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-tools/commi